{
  "id": "NAM.2",
  "number": "2",
  "bookId": "NAM",
  "reference": "Nahum 2",
  "verseCount": 13,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "2",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "NAM 2"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "2",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He that dasheth in pieces is come up against thee: keep the fortress, watch the way, make thy loins strong, fortify thy power mightily. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For Jehovah restoreth the excellency of Jacob, as the excellency of Israel; for the emptiers have emptied them out, and destroyed their vine-branches. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The shield of his mighty men is made red, the valiant men are in scarlet: the chariots flash with steel in the day of his preparation, and the cypress ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " are brandished. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The chariots rage in the streets; they rush to and fro in the broad ways: the appearance of them is like torches; they run like the lightnings. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He remembereth his nobles: they stumble in their march; they make haste to the wall thereof, and the mantelet is prepared. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The gates of the rivers are opened, and the palace is dissolved. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And it is decreed: she is uncovered, she is carried away; and her handmaids moan as with the voice of doves, beating upon their breasts.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Nineveh hath been from of old like a pool of water: yet they flee away. Stand, stand, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "; but none looketh back. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Take ye the spoil of silver, take the spoil of gold; for there is no end of the store, the glory of all goodly furniture. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "She is empty, and void, and waste; and the heart melteth, and the knees smite together, and anguish is in all loins, and the faces of them all are waxed pale. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Where is the den of the lions, and the feeding-place of the young lions, where the lion ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " the lioness walked, the lion’s whelp, and none made them afraid? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The lion did tear in pieces enough for his whelps, and strangled for his lionesses, and filled his caves with prey, and his dens with ravin. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "NAM 2:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Behold, I am against thee, saith Jehovah of hosts, and I will burn her chariots in the smoke, and the sword shall devour thy young lions; and I will cut off thy prey from the earth, and the voice of thy messengers shall no more be heard.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "NAM.2.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "NAM.2.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
